commit 1b34b54d83a883996453fa26d1106fc7b754cb9e
Author:     InnoPeak <global_ai@innopeaktech.com>
AuthorDate: Wed May 20 11:38:18 2026 -0700
Commit:     InnoPeak <global_ai@innopeaktech.com>
CommitDate: Wed May 20 11:38:18 2026 -0700

    fix(plugin-organizer): atomic save, hydrate guard, URL roundtrip, folder inference (P1 C-group)
    
    Why:
    - Codex cross-vendor review on `codex/track-a-desktop-foundation` flagged
      four plugin-organizer correctness gaps that can silently corrupt user
      state. None block compilation today, but each becomes user-visible
      the moment the SQLite repo, real Finder drops, or URL items light up.
    
    What (B1) — repositoryLayoutStore.save is now transactional:
    - The grid upsert+cull and item upsert+cull loops now run inside
      `gridRepo.transaction(tx => ...)` and `itemRepo.transaction(tx => ...)`
      respectively. On the in-memory driver this is snapshot-atomic; on the
      Tauri SQLite driver (post-G2.6) it batches via db_put_batch. Failures
      still bubble through `onSaveError`, but partial writes never leak.
    
    What (B2) — useGridSystem hydrate cannot clobber user edits:
    - Added a `userTouched` ref initialised to `false` and flipped to `true`
      at the start of every user-facing mutation (`createGrid`,
      `updateGrid`, `toggleFold`, `deleteGrid`, `clearAll`, `moveItem`,
      `toggleLock`, `addItem`, `addItemToGrid`).
    - Inside the async hydrate, after the existing `cancelled` check, we
      now bail out if `userTouched.current === true`, emit a console.warn,
      and still flip `hydrated` so the debounced save effect persists the
      user's current state.
    
    What (B3) — URL items round-trip through DesktopItem without loss:
    - `DesktopItemType` is widened to include `"url"` (behaviour-preserving).
    - `DesktopItem` gains an optional `url?: { href; title?; description?;
      favicon? }` field mirroring the `GridItemEntity.url` shape.
    - `entityToDesktopItem` and `desktopItemToEntity` now preserve the url
      payload symmetrically. Previously `kind: "url"` was lossy-mapped to
      `type: "file"` and the URL metadata was dropped.
    
    What (B4) — inferKindFromPath recognises folders without trailing slashes:
    - Added optional second arg `opts?: { isDirectory?: boolean }` so callers
      with FS truth can pin the kind.
    - Strengthened heuristic: a basename with no `.` (and not ending in
      `.app`) now defaults to `folder` rather than `file`. Real Finder drops
      never include trailing slashes.
    
    Scope:
    - packages/plugin-organizer/src/layoutStore.ts
    - packages/plugin-organizer/src/useGridSystem.tsx
    - packages/plugin-organizer/src/types.ts
    - packages/plugin-organizer/src/gridItemFactory.ts
    - packages/plugin-organizer/src/layoutStore.test.ts (+2 tests)
    - packages/plugin-organizer/src/gridItemFactory.test.ts (+2 tests)
    - packages/plugin-organizer/src/useGridSystem.test.tsx (new, +1 test)
    - packages/plugin-organizer/package.json (devDeps: jsdom, @testing-library/react)
    - pnpm-lock.yaml
    
    Risk:
    - B3 widens the `DesktopItemType` union — purely additive, so existing
      callers (e.g. OrganizerLayer drop handler) still satisfy the type.
    - B4 changes the default for extensionless paths from `file` to
      `folder`. The previously-passing test case `/Users/me/Documents/file.txt`
      still resolves to `file` (has a dot); `Safari.app` still resolves to
      `app`. New tests cover the extensionless folder path.
    - Transactional save now requires the repo driver to honour
      `Repo.transaction`; both in-memory and Tauri drivers already do.
    
    Docs:
    - Inline comments on inferKindFromPath document the heuristic rule
      order. Behaviour notes on save() and hydrate guard explain why
      atomicity matters once `createTauriRepo` is wired.
    
    Tests:
    - pnpm --filter @repo/plugin-organizer test → 46 passing (was 41).
      - layoutStore.test.ts: +URL round-trip preservation, +rollback when
        cull throws.
      - gridItemFactory.test.ts: +folder inference without trailing slash,
        +isDirectory override beats extension heuristic.
      - useGridSystem.test.tsx: +late hydrate discarded when user touched
        state first (uses @testing-library/react under jsdom).
    - pnpm --filter @repo/plugin-organizer check-types → PASS.
    - pnpm --filter desktop build → PASS.
    
